  <iati-identifier>XM-DAC-41302-IP24-YEM155</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-41302" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Labour Organization (ILO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened policies and programmes on enterprises,  productivity and working conditions in SMEs, green jobs and cooperatives</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MSMEs in Yemen face significant challenges due to prolonged conflict, leading to slow recovery and reliance on international aid. Data shows that 35% of medium-sized businesses have shut down, small enterprises have a negative growth rate, and only 6% of adults have bank accounts. Despite this, the private sector remains vital, employing over 80% of the workforce, with significant roles in agriculture, fishing, services, and manufacturing.
The ILO aims to support MSMEs through a multi-dimensional package promoting inclusive entrepreneurship, value chain development, access to finance, and strengthened cooperatives. 
Additionally, the ILO seeks to boost the competitiveness and productivity of Yemen&apos;s coffee supply chain, which has potential for supporting peace and well-being. Coffee exports have declined due to conflict, low productivity, poor quality, inadequate institutional capacity, land use issues, water scarcity, and policy constraints. The ILO&#x2019;s intervention will target the entire coffee supply chain&#x2014;from production to export&#x2014;through comprehensive measures to enhance competitiveness and export potential, advancing decent work in Yemen.</narrative>
  </description>
